{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/142079-satch-tries-adjusting-mechanics","id":142079,"title":"Satch Tries Adjusting Mechanics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-18T22:12:45-07:00","id":142079,"title":"Satch Tries Adjusting Mechanics","content":"Nearing the end of my corebook reread (after which I begin rereading Book of the Dead and the assorted SASes [and possibly the relevant sections of bluebook stuff like Glimpses of the Unknown or Mirrors]), I'm thinking about tossing together a few general fixes to bring Geist's presented mechanics in line with the GMC update and otherwise tweak the game while staying in line with the presentation of the fiction and other details.<br /> <br /> Seeing as I'm approaching a couple of time-consuming other things, though, I'm mostly going to be doing this piecemeal, attaching rationales when I can. Feedback is appreciated.<br /> <br /> To begin:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Adjust the activation dicepool for Manifestations to Manifestation Attribute + Key Skill + Memento Bonus, removing the Manifestation dots from the calculation.<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> Incentivizes pursuit of stronger mementos at all levels of Manifestation proficiency. Additional Manifestation dots already provide bonuses in the form of new abilities or contributions to effect calculation, and the multiplicative progression of gaining new Keys and Manifestations has been observed to skew the perceived power level of the splat. Memento bonuses being Key-based retains the notion of thematic specialization.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Adjust the basic range progression of the Boneyard to a flat [successes]*100 yard radius, retaining any conditional expanders (i.e. add [Skill] to successes for range purposes).<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> It's the range provided by the middle dot in the as-written mechanics. The radius measured in miles combined with having five extra dice from the Manifestation dots produces another awkward multiplicative effect that skews the perception of the power.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> The basic Rage attack is now treated as a [dots]L attack, adhering to changes for specific Keys as already established.<br /> <b>Rationale:</b> Basic GMC damage update, subject to fiddling if this off-the-cuff tweak turns out to be ill-advised.<br /> <br /> More to come in the not-so-imminent future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T19:54:07-07:00","id":142974,"title":"","content":"Tentative tweaks on the Boneyard again:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Adjust the basic range of the Boneyard to a flat [successes]*10 yard radius for any Boneyard with a conditional expander. Conditional expanders now increase this to a [successes]*100 yard radius, which remains the basic range of Boneyards without such modifiers.<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> Further incentivizes use of Boneyards that affect the physical world in thematically resonant locations.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Change the bonus provided to unlocking same-Key Manifestations within a Boneyard to a flat boost of [Boneyard dots/2, round down, minimum +0].<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> Makes the bonus less of the point of the Boneyard. Reduces the problematic aspects of adding memento bonuses to an activation roll more than once (add bonus to Boneyard activation to get more successes to add to other Manifestation activation in addition to bonus from same memento).<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Allow the Boneyard to be sustained over multiple scenes by spending a point of plasm per additional scene, as the Marionette's mechanic.<br /> <b>Rationale:</b> Ups the story potential of the Boneyard as a long-term investigative tool.<br /> <br /> And some others:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Switch dot values of charm and vanitas mementos.<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> Utility and replaceability of charms are higher and lower, respectively, than vanitas. Increases value of charms as emergency healing over that provided by draining something you're not supposed to destroy personally. Clusters together mementos that have Keys.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Allow Archetypal Manifestations to be performed once per chapter instead of once per story, hooking this into the Beat mechanics for dramatic failure.<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> More dramatic failures are a good thing. More encouragement to act within one's Archetype is a good thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Base effect of the Shroud is now providing [dots/2 round up] points of general Armor and [dots/2 round down] points of ballistic Armor.<br /> <b>Rationale:</b> Basic GMC armor update, subject to fiddling if this off-the-cuff tweak turns out to be ill-advised.<br /> <br /> As always, feedback is appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T22:35:45-07:00","id":143112,"title":"","content":"I'm liking these changes. I keep going back and forth over whether I want something more different for a GMC update or something closer to the original material, and I think these hacks do a great job of covering the latter.<br /> <br /> Do you have any thoughts on how Synergy should change, if at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T22:49:57-07:00","id":143121,"title":"","content":"I also like the changes, so keep up the good work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T23:26:26-07:00","id":143140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/142079-satch-tries-adjusting-mechanics?p=143112#post143112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any thoughts on how Synergy should change, if at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the moment the bulk of my thoughts on Synergy amount to &quot;god I hope Idigam Chronicle comes out way sooner than expected so I can shamelessly steal from Harmony&quot; because these are stopgap measures and I find it an amusing coincidence that the sample characters from New York have Synergy ratings that almost seem to have been set under the assumption that that was how it worked.<br /> <br /> I will probably have more refined thoughts on the subject as time goes on, but for the moment I'm content to pin a sketch to the wall that says &quot;Synergy 0 is all-dead, Synergy 10 is too-alive, Synergy 5 is the Goldilocks zone&quot; and go back to picking at Manifestations and ghosts. Speaking of which:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Any ghost that has made its &quot;home&quot; in the Underworld (i.e. has picked up a ratty black/white/brown/gray/drab shroud and has lost its original anchors) automatically gains the abilities of the Consume Offering Numen, which is treated as a part of being a ghost that does not manifest outside the Underworld for reasons of only having an effect in the Underworld.<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> &quot;Can drink from the Rivers or eat ofrendas to get Essence&quot; really doesn't have any business staying a Numen in post-GMC where ghosts no longer naturally accrue Numina and have a limited number by Rank. The mechanics of the Numen are functionally similar to spirits' Essence regeneration, which is an innate quality, so it's only fitting that this also be an innate quality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T03:04:13-07:00","id":143255,"title":"","content":"Looking pretty decent, so far. My only two hick-ups is with the Boneyard range, and Shroud. The fact that you've effectively reduced the max-range of the boneyard, i mean. Maybe if you performed some kind of sacrifice or death-themed ritual while in your thematic setting, you could crank it back up to the miles range?<br /> And the general nerf to the Shroud is also a thing. Armor has gotten pretty badass, so a 5/5 armor now, is crazy powerful. But do you think a straight nerf is the best way to go?<br /> <br /> Anyway, its looking good. I'm looking forward to what you come up with for Synergy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T19:35:53-07:00","id":145151,"title":"","content":"Are you sure that'd be the ideal for Synergy? I think it's excellent for representing the inherent, dualistic nature of the Werewolf, but unlike the Werewolf, Synergy doesn't seem like it lends itself to being &quot;too man&quot; or &quot;too geist&quot; but rather to a linear model which depicts how well the two work in concert. It isn't a measure of dualistic identity as much as it is synchronous existence. Either you're working in sync or you're out of sync.<br /> <br /> Just offering that as a thought.<br /> <br /> I think making that Numen inherent to Ghosts makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> How would you handle Geists channeling Numina? Roughly the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T20:59:42-07:00","id":145248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/142079-satch-tries-adjusting-mechanics?p=143255#post143255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe if you performed some kind of sacrifice or death-themed ritual while in your thematic setting, you could crank it back up to the miles range?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, one of the things that I contemplated back when the rereading progress was at the Manifestations was changing the Boneyard to a Ceremony flavored by one of your Keys (hey, Dedicate Charm's got it) or a Bedlam-esque innate ability unlocked by high Psyche. All told, though, the mile range-band is only open at the very last dot and I can't determine much in the way of justification given that the distances involved frequently exceed the narrative utility of such a large region. The Boneyard's schtick is broad spooky action at a distance within an area mixed with domain-sense-y scrying within that scope, but past a certain radius that stops looking like a good call.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the general nerf to the Shroud is also a thing. Armor has gotten pretty badass, so a 5/5 armor now, is crazy powerful. But do you think a straight nerf is the best way to go? </div> </div> </div>As far as this goes I can only blame it being 2AM for my misremembering how the stopgap Mage Armor progression I was using as a model worked. Accordingly:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack</b>: Base effect of the Shroud is now providing [dots] points of general Armor and [dots/2 round down] points of ballistic Armor.<br /> <b>Rationale:</b> As above, subjected and still subject to fiddling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/142079-satch-tries-adjusting-mechanics?p=145151#post145151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure that'd be the ideal for Synergy? I think it's excellent for representing the inherent, dualistic nature of the Werewolf, but unlike the Werewolf, Synergy doesn't seem like it lends itself to being &quot;too man&quot; or &quot;too geist&quot; but rather to a linear model which depicts how well the two work in concert. It isn't a measure of dualistic identity as much as it is synchronous existence. Either you're working in sync or you're out of sync.<br /> <br /> Just offering that as a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should like to note both that Synergy is a measure of balance as much as unity - the resurrection mechanics in particular note the revival shifts that balance of power toward the geist as a rationale for the loss of Synergy and maximum Synergy - and that Harmony could as easily be said to be &quot;you're either in tune with your exalted predatory nature or you're not&quot; under the old system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would you handle Geists channeling Numina? Roughly the same? </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about Fetters, my current standby is to wait until details emerge about how IC or FWC treat fetishes, but the general framework of &quot;spend a WP and use an appropriate Attribute+Skill pool to get about the same effect&quot; seems sound, after accounting for tricky matters like Possession no longer being a Numen and Influences being a thing.<br /> <br /> I'm likely going to save particular tweaks for after I've gone over the broader mechanics, which may take some time; I have a ten-book fantasy series to read by week after next alongside catching up with some shows and negotiating work and family matters, and it's kind of splitting my focus. For the time being, a few gimmes:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Rather than having a largely nonfunctional Psyche score, unBound geister have a Rank of 3 or more.<br /> <b>Rationale:</b> Pretty much what we've been told is the case already.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Rather than having Keys that add three dice to rolls involving particular Skills, geister treat those uses of their Keys as actions relating directly to their concept, rolling Attribute + Rank instead of Attribute alone.<br /> <b>Rationale: </b>Cuts down on fiddly clutter bits.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Rather than losing Power from crossing Rivers, Kerberoi lose Rank, capping their Traits accordingly.<br /> <b>Rationale: </b>Apart from the fiddly aspect of capping the level of Manifestations the Kerberoi can replicate, this is somewhat tidier.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Wherever the text references derangements, instead apply an identical Condition.<br /> <b>Rationale: </b>General systems update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T15:39:24-07:00","id":146096,"title":"","content":"Oh, just remembered an important one:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Ghosts that have anchors can still enter the Underworld.<br /> <b>Rationale:</b> Anchors being changed to Influences makes losing them less of an irreversible threshold.<br /> <br /> And as more of a note/supposition than an actual definite change:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Ghosts in the Underworld can change some of their Influence dots as a function of giving up memories in assorted chthonic transactions (e.g. ferrymen bribes, Old Laws, etc.) A ghost who replaces all of their Influences with things exclusive to the Underworld can no longer stave off Essence bleed in the mortal world save through rituals drawing on their personal identity in general or plot-device mechanisms such as unique cosmological confluences or special dispensation from the Kerberoi; none of their Influences work as Anchors.<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> Feeds into the notion that ghosts in the Underworld are changed by the place, draws a sharp delineation between ghosts who have completely assimilated into Underworld cultures (and the Kerberoi) and those who still meddle in the mortal realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T17:55:41-07:00","id":146224,"title":"","content":"If a Ghost loses all instances of the Anchor Condition for itself, it gets sent down to the Underworld. Does the nature of its Essence gain/loss change once there, or does it require them to exchange influences like they do in the Underworld as per the Hack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T18:10:58-07:00","id":146229,"title":"","content":"Had a realization that necessitates clarification:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Ghosts that have &quot;active&quot; (Conditioned to Open or beyond) anchors can still enter the Underworld, but cannot cross the Rivers without losing (here defined as at least dropping it back to Anchor) at least one per River to be crossed (or all of them, whichever is lower).<br /> <b>Rationale:</b> The Underworld as a place for ghosts to go through to reach their final reward means the places where ghosts are most likely to find new purposes ought to be barred from ghosts who still cling to life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/142079-satch-tries-adjusting-mechanics?p=146224#post146224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Ghost loses all instances of the Anchor Condition for itself, it gets sent down to the Underworld. Does the nature of its Essence gain/loss change once there, or does it require them to exchange influences like they do in the Underworld as per the Hack?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter; the ghost's Corpus shifts aesthetically with that first disconnection-induced visit, but being fresh from the living world means it's still got the memory of life to focus on. Generally speaking the ghost doesn't lose the ability to regain Essence from remembrance until it loses the ability to be recognized as the person it once was, which generally won't happen for quite some time but acts as enough of a loss of viable influx that Consume Offering becomes the more practical go-to means of recovery.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I'm still on the fence about what to do with Sin Feeder. Anybody care to weigh in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-23-2014, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T05:53:20-07:00","id":146615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/142079-satch-tries-adjusting-mechanics?p=146229#post146229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had a realization that necessitates clarification:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Ghosts that have &quot;active&quot; (Conditioned to Open or beyond) anchors can still enter the Underworld, but cannot cross the Rivers without losing (here defined as at least dropping it back to Anchor) at least one per River to be crossed (or all of them, whichever is lower).<br /> <b>Rationale:</b> The Underworld as a place for ghosts to go through to reach their final reward means the places where ghosts are most likely to find new purposes ought to be barred from ghosts who still cling to life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, honestly, this one is going to far. Allowing ghosts that still have anchors into the underworld at all kind of changes the dynamic of ghosts anchors: they're now a boon strictly speaking, while some might prefer that they're something the ghost might eventually despise - something that chains them to the mortal life they can no longer have. Giving them a way to let go of the things they love without having to do something drastic to a thing they love kind of kills a lot of story opportunities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T06:33:21-07:00","id":146630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/142079-satch-tries-adjusting-mechanics?p=146615#post146615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think, honestly, this one is going to far. Allowing ghosts that still have anchors into the underworld at all kind of changes the dynamic of ghosts anchors: they're now a boon strictly speaking, while some might prefer that they're something the ghost might eventually despise - something that chains them to the mortal life they can no longer have. Giving them a way to let go of the things they love without having to do something drastic to a thing they love kind of kills a lot of story opportunities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I note that:<br /> <br /> 1) Avernian Gates still largely open in circumstances that are little better than chance for most ghosts.<br /> <br /> 2) Most ghosts only have one or two Anchors in the first place, which may be destroyed by simple entropy if they make a jaunt down into the Autochthonous Depths and don't get out before the door shuts.<br /> <br /> 3) Not all ghosts' Anchors represent unfinished business, and the GMC mechanics in general seem to be moving toward an assumption that ghosts are a little more durable existence-wise than earlier mechanics indicated.<br /> <br /> 4) The Autochthonous Depths are many things, but I am having some difficulty picturing them as a place the average spook would relish being trapped for an indefinite period of time, anchors or none.<br /> <br /> 5) The Underworld being a place where ghosts shed their attachments to the mortal world, combined with the earlier hack's stipulation that only naturalized ghosts pick up Consume Offering, means ghosts that still have Anchors are severely curtailed in their ability to regain Essence along with their broad-scale mobility unless time and tide erode their grip.<br /> <br /> 6) Avernian Gate is now a ghost-accessible Manifestation Effect and our one example so far who has it is not noted as having changed much.<br /> <br /> 7) Non-compulsionary ghost-summoning necessarily generates the Anchor Condition, which, while only giving the ghost the option of answering the summons, still works for ghosts in the Underworld, which rather puts the lie to &quot;if you have Anchors at all you can't enter the Underworld&quot; in the new context of Anchors (and the existing summoning mechanics only work on ghosts in the Autochthonous Depths from the Autochthonous Depths).<br /> <br /> 8) A keystone memento is specifically mentioned as a means of &quot;safeguarding against the destruction of the final anchor&quot; and geister are the most mobile things in the Underworld and its surrounding environs.<br /> <br /> 9) The hack is &quot;you can't cross the Rivers without losing your Anchors,&quot; not &quot;crossing the Rivers loses you your Anchors.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-23-2014, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T22:40:05-07:00","id":147623,"title":"","content":"Are any of the Sin-Eater's inherent abilities in need of hacks? Stuff like Death Stains, infusing ghosts with plasm, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T22:14:30-07:00","id":152140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/142079-satch-tries-adjusting-mechanics?p=147623#post147623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are any of the Sin-Eater's inherent abilities in need of hacks? Stuff like Death Stains, infusing ghosts with plasm, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Opening Avernian Gates needs the modifiers from Synergy adjusted, resurrection needs clarified and the Synergy costs given a look-over, and plasmic infusion can afford a more elegant solution than &quot;treat them as though they had an Intelligence equal to their Power,&quot; among other things. A quick particular or two:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Sin-Eaters can automatically detect any place that has held the Resonant [Death] Condition within the last decade as a function of their ability to sense Death Stains.<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> The penalty goes up by one for every year since the death, the dicepool for analysis is relatively small, and while the wording is vague a case can be made for &quot;penalty greater than -10 stops the power working&quot; being the operative precedent.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Sin-Eaters can specifically detect Avernian Gates through their morbid senses.<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> Gives the system of marking Avernian Gates a little more nuance; Sin-Eaters are more likely to bother to mark a gate to indicate particulars about the region of the Depths it opens up into, like warning signs; more general &quot;deadlands found here&quot; signs are thus more likely the work of the more plentiful mortal occultists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T22:49:39-07:00","id":152160,"title":"","content":"I've been toying around with similar ideas. I too plan on looting the new Harmony system for Synergy. As such, I already had an idea as to how to handle resurrection penalties.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> The first time a Sin-Eater is resurrected, he loses the 5th dot of Synergy. Cross it out. The character can never have Synergy at 5 again. After subsequent resurrections, he loses 6 and 4, then 7 and 3, etc. Eventually, the character has only dots 10 and 0 remaining. After each resurrection, the character automatically moves one step toward 0.<br /> <b>Rationale:</b> This captures the feel of loosing to very possibility of balance. When reduced to only 10 and 0, the slightest bit of discord sends the character careening to the other extreme. This gets the feel of the Wretched as presented in the book as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T22:15:51-07:00","id":158717,"title":"","content":"Have finished reading Book of the Dead, Through the Ebon Gate, The House Always Wins, Dem Bones, and the Geist section of Glimpses of the Unknown, and am now looking through Second Sight (because cited source for potential pre-Bargain powers and because useful cross-applicable advice for dealing with some of the same concepts as Geist covers) while trying to wrap up Psycho-Pass (because sin and punishment and spoilers). Accordingly, some (exceedingly rambly) notes:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> The Underworld absolutely <i>does</i> change - the deeper the more often - but such changes tend to take decades and significant numbers or varieties of death, significant shifts in culture, or special ceremonies akin to Funerary Tools to affect the Autochthonous Depths, and such changes do not impact the thresholds of the region - Avernian Gates still open where they did, the same Gates or Rivers are accessible as before, as are most unique landmarks. The regions most susceptible to these changes tend to be closest to the mortal world, where the tenor of the Depths mostly shifts very gradually in keeping with the local human concept of death. Generally speaking, however, a path will usually remain consistent as long as it is remembered or recorded as such, the further a region of the Depths strays from the Gates the older the concepts that give it its tenor tend to be, and the Underworld doesn't need to resort to changing the maze when natural pockets of drugged air are a potential hazard one might run across before or after a terrifying new sight sends one running without counting the tunnels.<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> Mictlan and the cathedral from Through the Ebon Gate are both deep-Underworld domains that are both mutable within a theme and under the control of a powerful deathly being. Much though I love the notion behind &quot;Foundations, not Reflections,&quot; if taken as a unilateral trait of Erebus it contradicts the established notion of New York's Underworld as having macabre facsimiles of subway tunnels along with the evocatively bizarre visual of having parts of manmade objects poking out of the walls, and there's only so much geographical culture bleed that can reasonably be chalked up to ghostly innovation. The Underworld is described in multiple places as though its terrain were not immutable - places are carved out of the rock, cave-ins happen, and presumably more things than just stray mortals and fresh air rush in when a cenote pops open anywhere other than a totally deserted abandoned mineshaft. Things like the Jack o' Lanterns' Necropolis and the mock-buried pavilion of Steeplechase Park, among others, point to the idea that entire buildings and places - or at least most of them - can be made to appear in the Underworld after their destruction. Nevertheless, the most mutable locations tend to have their most drastic shifts bound to a set domain, and most ghosts aren't equipped to carve away at the stone at a rate that can be measured in less than a mortal lifetime, so the primary threats to travelers using an &quot;outdated&quot; map are ghosts and other denizens or a thematic shift having brought new hazards to the passageways - a map from the time of a tomb-building society will not prepare its user for the risks that will have arrived with a cultural shift toward cremation, for example, even if the warped statuary it references has stayed there the entire time.<br /> <br /> I feel like this one needs refinement; any questions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T02:48:57-07:00","id":158862,"title":"","content":"Like it a lot. Maybe with the caveat that old domains does not just &quot;disappear&quot;, but they just sink &quot;down&quot;, in more and more hidden places of the Underworld. It is actually possible to arrive to an &quot;out of date&quot; domain, but you'll better dig a lot for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T17:34:49-07:00","id":159489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/142079-satch-tries-adjusting-mechanics?p=158862#post158862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like it a lot. Maybe with the caveat that old domains does not just &quot;disappear&quot;, but they just sink &quot;down&quot;, in more and more hidden places of the Underworld. It is actually possible to arrive to an &quot;out of date&quot; domain, but you'll better dig a lot for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, almost certainly; I continue to find the mention of a deathlord in Erra, Prime of Seven's writeup curious in its phrasing - &quot;an interminable slumber of <b>disuse</b>&quot; seems an odd way to refer to the most powerful personalities of the Underworld if one doesn't take into account other godly creatures of the World of Darkness like the Fae being capable of taking the forms of objects and places, but even in the same book as Erra appears we have references to the crushers of the Junkyard as the gods of their Dominion despite being little more than enormous smashing devices.<br /> <br /> A general note to account for Essence:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> In the absence of extenuating circumstances, ghosts in the Underworld are assumed to regain at least one point of Essence per scene from consumption, Vice, looking upon grave good ofrendas, theft, donation, and so on. As a broad guideline, the average Underworld-dwelling ghost gains their Rank in Essence per &quot;day&quot; (24-hour period) through means that require action on the part of the ghost.<br /> <b>Rationale(s): </b>General bookkeeping and accounting for the &quot;running out of Essence in the Underworld renders a ghost agonizingly intangible&quot; phenomenon.<br /> <br /> And a further update on anchors:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> The transformation of a ghost's Corpus to symbolize its assimilation into the structure of the Underworld is contingent upon the resolution (by destruction or exorcism or otherwise) of the last instance of the Anchor Condition created at the point of the ghost's generation while the ghost is prevented from suffering Essence Bleed due to that Condition (whether by physical proximity or a contingent Manifestation Effect).<br /> <b>Rationale(s):</b> It's still unclear whether the ability to jump between anchors with a point of Willpower is still a thing, but given the speed with which ghosts can move (accounting for the heightened species factor and the reduced amount of obstacles in Twilight) it seems reasonable to assume that losing one of multiple Anchors is unlikely to stymie a ghost from escaping to another one even if it hasn't grown to the point where it can redeclare an Anchor.<br /> <br /> Finally, pasting some of the original corebook's notes on anchors, as food for thought:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WoD Core Rulebook, p209, &quot;Anchors&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts linger in the physical world because something anchors them there, preventing them from continuing on to the spirit realm. Every ghost has at least one anchor rooting it to the physical world. Some powerful spirits may have more. The number and nature of a ghost's anchors depends on the individual and the circumstances surrounding its death. <b>In most cases, an anchor is a physical place or object that held <u>great emotional significance</u> to the ghost during its mortal existence.</b> An elderly woman who spent her last years largely confined to her bed might be anchored to the bedroom or to the bed itself. A man who carried a valuable pocket watch wherever he went might be a ghost anchored to the watch, haunting those who come to possess it. Occasionally, ghosts can be anchored to <i>people</i> rather than to objects. A father whose last thought was for the welfare of his children may be anchored to them, watching over them in death as he did in life. Or a woman murdered by a jilted lover may find her ghost anchored to him, sustained by a bitter desire for revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>And backing up the emphasis with bits from the sample fetter mementos from Geist:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The love for that dog kept John connected to the living world</b> \u2014 and a Sin-Eater bound his ghost to the collar of the dog.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> A child\u2019s ghost is troubled because it doesn\u2019t understand. Its consciousness is childish and underdeveloped. The good things are stripped from it, leaving it a tantrum-driven entity, <b>mired in its own misunderstood anger.</b><br /> [\u2026]<br /> Mary died from silicone poisoning at the age of 34, but her ghost remained, <b>tied to the world through her vanity.</b><br /> [\u2026]<br /> Lee\u2019s restless specter \u2014 <b>kept to the living world through his connection to the game and the other players within it</b> \u2014 now infuses the laptop.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> [Rose Neville's] ghost remained, <b>clinging to the dark emotions she left behind</b> and hovering about the small cache of films that lie behind a hidden wall along with her projector.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> After reading about the number of fatalities along the cliffs, a Sin-Eater put two and two together and managed to find the now rusty can of mace along the path and bind Jenny to it. Now, pressing the little tab at the top doesn\u2019t release a spray of chemicals. Instead, it releases <b>the pent up rage of Jenny</b> in a sonic shriek.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> His last thought before dying in hospice care was a deep and vile regret that he\u2019d never get to kill again. His ghost remained, <b>clinging to the living world with that lingering urge</b> \u2014 thankfully, some Sin-Eater was good enough to at least put the ghost out of commission (as Pitts\u2019 murderous spree would\u2019ve surely continued) by shackling it to one of Pitts\u2019 own anchors, the long flat-blade screwdriver that had served as his weapon for over 20 years. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T17:38:17-07:00","id":159491,"title":"","content":"Although it's from the Demon SAS, how do we reconcile the ghost there's lack of the Anchor Influence? Is Sadness just the kind of Anchor he has, or what's the deal? Was it just an oversight?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Reason I'm asking here is because the confusion might be helpful for figuring things out in Geist as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T20:08:39-07:00","id":159671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/142079-satch-tries-adjusting-mechanics?p=159491#post159491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although it's from the Demon SAS, how do we reconcile the ghost there's lack of the Anchor Influence? Is Sadness just the kind of Anchor he has, or what's the deal? Was it just an oversight?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Reason I'm asking here is because the confusion might be helpful for figuring things out in Geist as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/71851-unpacking-manifestation-conditions#post71851\">I've covered this elsewhere.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:03:45-07:00","id":165379,"title":"","content":"Once more with feeling re: Anchors, after giving another reread of the GMC Ephemera rules:<br /> <br /> <b>Hack: </b>Ghosts that with Anchors, whether their original ones or new ones gained through Influence or other magic, discorporate and reform at the nearest one to their position if they run out of Essence due to Essence Bleed.<br /> <b>Rationale(s): </b>The GMC notes on dormancy specify that ghosts <i>without anchors</i> are forced into the Underworld. Unlike Gauntlet Breach, Avernian Gateway is specified as opening an existing gate rather than simply pushing through a relevant Resonant Condition; thus, even if the ambiguity of &quot;Requires Open Condition&quot; for Avernian Gateway allowed it to be used through an Opened Anchor Condition, Avernian Gates don't appear at such locales without also having a resonance of Death that can be Opened.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Exorcism no longer categorically banishes a ghost to the Underworld; this only happens with the exorcism of the ghost's last anchor. Anchors suppressed by abjuration do not count as &quot;lost&quot; for the purposes of triggering the opening of Avernian Gates.<br /> <b>Rationale: </b>Change necessitated by changes to exorcism mechanics.<br /> <br /> <b>Hack:</b> Ghosts cannot enter the Underworld if they possess any of the anchors formed by their creation, or any formed in the meantime; as with Consume Offering, this changes once they have undergone the shift in their Corpus that signifies their incorporation into mechanisms of the Great Below.<br /> <b>Rationale: </b>Anchors aren't easily replaced, and the situations where this happens are generally plot elements in their own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}